# Modelfile for cs-actions:v1 — fine-tuned changelog → action synthesizer
#
# Two-stage build:
#   1. Backpropagate trains and registers the LoRA-on-base adapter:
#        backprop export ./output/lora --format gguf --quantization q4_k_m \
#            --ollama --ollama-name cs-actions-base
#   2. This Modelfile adds deployment configuration on top:
#        ollama create cs-actions:v1 -f Modelfile.cs-actions-v1
#
# Clean separation: backprop owns weights, this file owns deployment config.

FROM cs-actions-base

# ─── Inference parameters ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# temperature 0.0 — Deterministic classification + extraction. Same input →
# byte-identical output, free caching. The model commits early on structured
# JSON output; temp > 0 would only break ties between near-equally-valid
# labels — which is the qwen3:8b cross-family verifier's job to surface, not
# the model's job to randomize internally. See EVAL.md for the verifier
# pipeline.
PARAMETER temperature 0.0

# num_predict 320 — Measured ceiling. Longest assistant message in
# training.jsonl tokenizes to 237 tokens via the Qwen2.5 BPE; 320 = ~35%
# headroom over max. Tighter than the 400 originally drafted; any output
# past this is the model degenerating into repetition, not legitimate JSON.
PARAMETER num_predict 320

# repeat_penalty 1.0 — Disabled (Ollama default is 1.1). Structured JSON
# output has legitimate token repetition (`"`, `,`, ` `, `{`, `}`) that a
# nonzero penalty would distort even under greedy sampling, biasing the
# logits toward fewer/different separators. Explicit 1.0 = off.
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.0

# top_p / top_k intentionally omitted — inert at temperature 0.0 (greedy
# sampling ignores nucleus / top-k filtering). Adding them as identity
# values would only be visual noise; the deterministic-greedy contract
# lives in `temperature 0.0` alone.

# ─── System prompt ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Byte-identical to manifest.json's `system_prompt` field. The dataset locks
# this string as part of the v1 contract — any drift requires a v2 dataset
# and a v2 fine-tune. Do not edit without bumping the model major version.
SYSTEM """You synthesize one changelog entry into one structured action item. Output strict JSON with fields: kind (one of: breaking | deprecation | security | feature | fix | performance | docs | unknown), severity (one of: low | medium | high), subject, action_text (verb-first imperative, 1-3 sentences, names the affected surface in backticks, max 500 chars), deadline (YYYY-MM-DD if upstream-named, else null), tags. Use kind='unknown' when you cannot classify confidently. Never invent deadlines."""

# ─── Callers MUST pass `format: "json"` per request ──────────────────────────
#
# Ollama's `format=json` parameter is per-request on /api/generate and
# /api/chat — it CANNOT be set as a Modelfile PARAMETER. Without it, the
# model's output is freeform text that happens to look like JSON; ~5-10%
# of outputs will carry stray markdown fences, prose preamble, or truncated
# braces and break JSON.parse downstream.
#
# Every caller of cs-actions:v1 must pass format=json. The eval harness
# does this explicitly (see EVAL.md). Any MCP tool wrapping this model
# must do the same. This is the one deployment-guarantee that lives in
# the caller, not the Modelfile.
